# Documentation layout

- Do not create planning, release, agent-brief, or checklist markdown at the
  repository root. Put it under `docs/` using
  `docs/README.md` (directory map).
- Only these four trackers live directly under `docs/`:
  `SSCRE_PLAN.md`, `SSCRE_PROJECT_ANALYSIS.md`,
  `SSCRE_LEARNING_AND_EXECUTION_GUIDE.md`, `SSCRE_SYSTEM_DESIGN.md`.
- Use `docs/internal/` for release prep and private briefs, `docs/reference/`
  for technical specs, `docs/setup/` for environment setup, `docs/phase-1/` and
  `docs/phase-2/` for milestone and workstream material.
- Keep new Phase 2 filenames in `docs/phase-2/` (flat folder). Code and
  benchmarks reference those paths; do not nest phase-2 files without updating
  every reference.
- When adding a notable file under `docs/phase-1/`, `docs/phase-2/`, or
  `docs/internal/`, add a row to that folder's `README.md` index.
- When moving or renaming docs, search the repo for the old path and update
  links in markdown, Python docstrings, and JSON metadata.
